0	section	Talking to Mary
1	line	Player	Hello there. Are you Mary?
1	line	Mary	That's right. Who are you?
1	line	Player	I'm {player}. Your husband told me that some beast has been causing you both trouble. I've agreed to kill it and bring back its head!
1	line	Mary	Ah, that's good to hear. We've already lost a lot of livestock to it.
1	line	Player	Well fear not. I'm sure I'll make short work of it. I do have one issue, however.
1	line	Mary	What's that?
1	line	Player	I don't yet know where to find this beast. I was wondering if you'd seen anything?
1	line	Mary	I'm afraid not. It only ever comes in the night, so we haven't been able to get a proper look at it.
1	line	Player	Hmm. This is a problem.
1	line	Mary	Well let's see now...
1	line	Mary	Oh! I have an idea! If this beast ended up getting coated in flour, it wouldn't be hard for you to track it back to its home.
1	line	Player	But how would I get it coated in flour?
1	line	Mary	Oh come on now! You're the adventurer here! Why don't you use your head?
1	line	Player	Use my head? Wait... Did you just...?
1	line	Mary	I don't know what you mean.
1	line	Player	Hmm...
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Mary again
1	line	Mary	Hello there. How goes the headhunt?
1	line	Player	I'm still trying to come up with a way to cover the beast in flour.
1	line	Mary	Well I'm sure you'll think of something. Just remember to use your head.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Sergeant
1	line	Player	Hello. Do you know anything about the beast causing trouble around here?
1	line	Sergeant	The farmers mentioned it. We haven't seen anything though. Our focus is on the lizardmen.
1	line	Player	Surely you'd notice a big beast wondering around though?
1	line	Sergeant	The farmers said it came at night. We're not on shift then.
1	line	Player	But then who's guarding the farm at night?
1	line	Sergeant	That's not our problem. We're just here to follow orders.
1	line	Player	Fine. I'll find the beast myself.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Gordon after talking to Mary
1	line	Gordon	Hello again. Any luck finding that beast?
1	line	Player	I've been trying, but I haven't made much progress yet.
1	line	Gordon	Anything you need from me?
1	line	Player	Just one question. You said this beast has been going for your livestock. Which animals has it been targeting?
1	line	Gordon	It's mainly been going for the cattle. I fixed up a new gate which has kept it out the past couple of nights. Not sure how long it will hold though.
1	line	Player	I see. Thanks for the information.
1	action	end
